# Files the Shopify CLI will NOT upload on `theme push`.
# Anything listed here stays whatever the live store already has.

# Repo/tooling files — not part of the theme
.git/*
.gitignore
.theme-check.yml
shopify.theme.toml
README.md
CLAUDE.md
*.zip
node_modules/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merchant-editable content. These files are rewritten every time someone saves
# in the Shopify theme editor. Pushing them would silently revert live
# customizations, so the theme editor stays their owner — not git.
#
# Consequence to remember: a NEW section added in code will not appear on any
# page until someone places it once via the theme editor. That is expected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config/settings_data.json
templates/*.json
